| Image | \`ghcr.io/acme/shop\` (GitHub Container Registry) |
| Database | PostgreSQL in the app's stack, data in the volume \`opscrew-shop_db_data\` |

## How a change reaches your Portainer

- Every push to \`main\` runs \`.github/workflows/opscrew-deploy.yml\`: it builds the image, pushes it to GitHub Container Registry and writes \`compose.yaml\` with the new image to the \`opscrew-deploy\` branch.
- The updater stack \`opscrew-shop-updater\` asks your Portainer once a minute, over the local network, to redeploy \`opscrew-shop\` from that branch when it changed.
- The workflow reports success only once the site answers its health check with the new version; otherwise it writes the previous image back to the \`opscrew-deploy\` branch, so the previous version returns.

